+## Multidestination Studio
+
+When the [Multidestination Studio](https://github.com/sebts-574/multidestination-studio) OBS plugin
+is installed, the connection detects it and adds a **Multidestination Studio** preset section. These
+buttons drive the plugin's studio (every destination) instead of the OBS main canvas:
+
+- **Scene to Preview** / **Scene to Program**: one button per scene, green in Preview, red in Program.
+- **Transition**: takes the studio Preview to Program with the current transition.
+- **Transition With**: one button per OBS transition, which takes the Preview with that transition.
+- **After a Transition** and **Destinations Shown**: toggles for the two studio settings, lit when on.
+- **Cue to Preview** and **Stop Cue**, when the plugin's Cues feature is on.
+
+The matching actions and feedbacks are listed under "Multidestination Studio". They use the plugin's
+vendor requests (vendor `multidestination-studio`) and refresh on its `StateChanged` vendor event.
+
